{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950626-what-would-a-person-with-one-dot-of-intelligence-but-four-dots-of-wits-be-like","id":950626,"title":"What would a person with one dot of intelligence but four dots of wits be like?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-14T10:29:33-07:00","id":950626,"title":"What would a person with one dot of intelligence but four dots of wits be like?","content":"Just for fun, they also have five dots of firearms and a firearms specialty in 'theory'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T10:35:23-07:00","id":950630,"title":"","content":"Very logic oriented but not able to make leaps of said logic. They could be good at planning things, bad at improvising. Relatively unobservant as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T10:38:14-07:00","id":950631,"title":"","content":"Or the reverse? I said one dot of intelligence and four of wits.<br /> <br /> I suppose I'm trying to figure out what a person with subpar intelligence but gifted wits would sound like? What would they understand and what would interest them? How does their specialty in firearms theory manifest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T10:55:04-07:00","id":950640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950626-what-would-a-person-with-one-dot-of-intelligence-but-four-dots-of-wits-be-like?p=950631#post950631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or the reverse? I said one dot of intelligence and four of wits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow yes, I completely misread that. Sorry. The opposite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I suppose I'm trying to figure out what a person with subpar intelligence but gifted wits would sound like? What would they understand and what would interest them? How does their specialty in firearms theory manifest. </div> </div> </div>Without the Firearms I played a character similarly, though I eventually upped the Intelligence to two because with 1 the Storyteller deemed he couldn't use basic things like Computers without a roll.<br /> <br /> But at that point you're talking about the kind of character that, in movies, would make leaps in logic that turned out right, without knowing much about what's going on, or the specifics. Something like, perhaps, Inspector Clouseau.<br /> <br /> Their interests aren't really limited, though I'd stay away from Intelligence-heavy tasks, but even that's not a definite. The high Wits means you have high Perception, and you are likely to notice important things. Since it's a group-oriented game the character noticing things is likely to help the rest of the team figure stuff out, even if the original character did not.<br /> <br /> Firearms theory sounds more like they have ideas for the design of firearms rather than anything that might help in combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T10:59:32-07:00","id":950643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950626-what-would-a-person-with-one-dot-of-intelligence-but-four-dots-of-wits-be-like?p=950640#post950640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Firearms theory sounds more like they have ideas for the design of firearms rather than anything that might help in combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, good point! So they know a ton about the theory of firearms but it comes across less as a sound understanding and more as 'I remember this really cool gun, that has x...'. Solving problems but never inspiring confidence that they could so again. That could be this characters tagline. :P<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T10:59:36-07:00","id":950644,"title":"","content":"Honestly, this game doesn't really work with 1 in a Attribute as &quot;terrible&quot;. Best way to portray someone truly bad in some aspect is to apply a Persistent Condition that would work like old-wod flaw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T12:57:24-07:00","id":950702,"title":"","content":"Forest Gump and Bubba. Forest was an idiot who made good personal decisions just because it seemed like the right thing to do, and Bubba knew everything there was to know about shrimp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T13:11:20-07:00","id":950710,"title":"","content":"You can show this multiple ways - 1 means 'bad', not necessarily ;idiot', though you could take it that way. They might also be a clearly smart person who was poorly educated and is a little impulsive, some kind of... gunfighting savant (not keen on his personally), someone incapable of long-term thinking but brilliant in the moment (I'm thinking Mr Tulip, for any Pratchett fans)...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T13:56:12-07:00","id":950733,"title":"","content":"Someone who isn't very intellectually-minded, but makes excellent use of the knowledge they have. In MBTI terms, strong Perceiving and Feeling functions, weak Thinking and Judging functions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T14:03:12-07:00","id":950736,"title":"","content":"Bugs Bunny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T14:12:45-07:00","id":950740,"title":"","content":"A 1 doesn't even mean, &quot;bad&quot; it just means, &quot;below average.&quot;<br /> <br /> I feel like there's a tendency to overstate the in-character extent of how bad being &quot;below average,&quot; is, because Attributes are described on a 1-5 scale, with 3-5 all being &quot;above average,&quot; leaving the impression that a 1 has to carry everything from &quot;C- student,&quot; to, &quot;bumbling idiot that can't figure out how to tie their own shoe laces,&quot; and disregard <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a> making the proper case that anything below the &quot;C- student,&quot; level of bad at Intelligence should be handled via the Conditions system.<br /> <br /> Someone with no Conditions and Intelligence 1/Wits 4, would most likely be someone others see as, &quot;book dumb, street smart.&quot; Outside of academic and scientific arenas, most people would see them as competent and conversant in practical matters; even if things like theory and trivia are probably things they don't know well.<br /> <br /> Adding in the Firearms specialty of &quot;theory&quot; is a bit odd (what does that even do?), but actually makes me think of Archer. Sterling is pretty stereotypical (if comedic because of the nature of the show) of what low Int/high Wits can look like (even if his Wits isn't has high as he likes to think it is) with high Firearms and some strange specialties. A good example is his ability to identify the guns other people are firing, and track bullet counts in the middle of highly chaotic situations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T14:19:24-07:00","id":950744,"title":"","content":"Ricky from the super popular canadian/netflix show Trailer Park Boys<br /> Dumb as a box of rocks but an ingenious um.. gardener who can think on his feet really fast so he can talk his way out of tickets, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1824-xaielao","name":"Xaielao","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1824_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T03:48:58-07:00","id":951583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950626-what-would-a-person-with-one-dot-of-intelligence-but-four-dots-of-wits-be-like?p=950740#post950740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A 1 doesn't even mean, &quot;bad&quot; it just means, &quot;below average.&quot;<br /> <br /> I feel like there's a tendency to overstate the in-character extent of how bad being &quot;below average,&quot; is, because Attributes are described on a 1-5 scale, with 3-5 all being &quot;above average,&quot; leaving the impression that a 1 has to carry everything from &quot;C- student,&quot; to, &quot;bumbling idiot that can't figure out how to tie their own shoe laces,&quot; and disregard <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a> making the proper case that anything below the &quot;C- student,&quot; level of bad at Intelligence should be handled via the Conditions system.<br /> <br /> Someone with no Conditions and Intelligence 1/Wits 4, would most likely be someone others see as, &quot;book dumb, street smart.&quot; Outside of academic and scientific arenas, most people would see them as competent and conversant in practical matters; even if things like theory and trivia are probably things they don't know well.<br /> <br /> Adding in the Firearms specialty of &quot;theory&quot; is a bit odd (what does that even do?), but actually makes me think of Archer. Sterling is pretty stereotypical (if comedic because of the nature of the show) of what low Int/high Wits can look like (even if his Wits isn't has high as he likes to think it is) with high Firearms and some strange specialties. A good example is his ability to identify the guns other people are firing, and track bullet counts in the middle of highly chaotic situations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I second this view. You're 'below average'; if you're playing a truly terrible character, that's better represented through Conditions.<br /> <br /> For example, grabbing this Condition from a brilliant GM in a game I am playing (Requiem-Masquerade):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Unskilled</b><br /> <br /> Your character is naturally bad at something. Choose a single Skill or Skill Specialty, such as Expression (Singing) or Subterfuge (Lying). Your character always rolls a chance die on rolls with this Skill or Skill Specialty, no matter how high a dice pool his Attributes would normally entitle him to. This Condition can be paired with the Delusional Condition to make a character wildly overestimate his abilities and believe he is an expert at something he\u2019s terrible at.<br /> <br /> Resolution: Your character works to overcome his deficiency and purchases a Skill dot or Specialty for the relevant Skill.<br /> <br /> Beat: You fail a roll for the Skill or Specialty you are deficient at.<br /> <br /> GM\u2019s Notes: This Condition is intended to model characters who are bad at something but have high enough Attributes to compensate for it. In one Vampire: The Masquerade setting book, there was an elder Toreador who was a poseur and a catastrophically terrible artist. His superhuman Presence and Dexterity dot ratings meant he was still better at the arts than most mortals, even factoring in the -1 untrained penalty for no dots in Expression. </div> </div> </div>You could possibly tailor the above to Attributes instead, for example making any call for a Strength roll would automatically be a Chance Die (signifying an elderly, decrepit character that is infirm - this in comparison to just having one-dot in the Attribute that simply means the character has a weak handshake or can't open a jar if it's too tight).<br /> <br /> As for my broader thoughts on what a one represents in the game-space:<br /> <br /> 1 Intelligence = unintelligent, forgetful, poor at academia<br /> 1 Wits = it makes the character a meat-head / bimbo, not very perceptive<br /> 1 Resolve = lazy, unmotivated, easily distracted or mentally taxed<br /> <br /> 1 Strength = weakling (seen a character take 1 Strength and the GM represent this as him having a limp handshake)<br /> 1 Dexterity = clumsy, uncoordinated<br /> 1 Stamina = fat, thin, unfit, soft like a marshmallow<br /> <br /> 1 Presence = unremarkable, plain, boring<br /> 1 Manipulation = ineloquent, inarticulate, uncogent<br /> 1 Composure = anxious, easily perturbed, shy, again not very perceptive<br /> <br /> If you want to tailor the above Condition to each of the above attributes to be automatic Chance Die, I'd title it as:<br /> <br /> Intelligence = Amnesic<br /> Wits = Witless<br /> Resolve = Listless<br /> <br /> Strength = Infirm<br /> Dexterity = Ungainly<br /> Stamina = Frail<br /> <br /> Presence = Unlikable<br /> Manipulation = Incoherent<br /> Composure = Meek<br /> <br /> edit: The way I think about it, the average person / mortal is deficient in at least one attribute (worthy of one-dot). Something to consider when populating your world with NPCs is that they're more likely to have mostly 2s and a 1 in their attributes as opposed to having a 3+ in any of their attributes. A three to me is somewhat remarkable, like a person with Intelligence 3 is notably book-smart and Presence 3 is notably charismatic (in the context of people you meet in your day-to-day life). Four is notable enough to garner celebrity. Five is freakish.<br /> <br /> 3 = one of the best in your city<br /> 4 = one of the best in your country<br /> 5 = one of the best in the world","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1592,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","user":"Jack","date":". 08-16-2016, 07:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T09:41:38-07:00","id":951784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950626-what-would-a-person-with-one-dot-of-intelligence-but-four-dots-of-wits-be-like?p=950740#post950740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A 1 doesn't even mean, &quot;bad&quot; it just means, &quot;below average.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>And an IQ of 60 is decidedly below average. To the point such an individual can't face judiciary proceedings like the average individual in some jurisdictions.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T10:35:49-07:00","id":951823,"title":"","content":"Did 2nd ED map certain IQ thresholds to stats? I know that new core gave some descriptions for specific skill levels, but I didn't see anything like that for Attributes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T10:42:38-07:00","id":951826,"title":"","content":"I'm sure if they did there would be a thread pointing out the problems of measuring Intelligence.<br /> <br /> But Malus is right. Incredibly low ability is below average. It's far below average, but it's still technically there. The book doesn't make a point to clarify where on the scale of below average 1 dot is. Having it just mean 'still capable but just below average' is warranted as much as 'able but only barely.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-16-2016, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T12:53:09-07:00","id":951941,"title":"","content":"As I noted in my post, there's an issue with there only being one rating for &quot;below average,&quot; in that it means 1 dot covers the biggest range of possible interpretations of the Attributes. The books would be better served calling out that filling in the gap between 0 and 1 should be done with Conditions rather than leaving it to readers to figure out.<br /> <br /> I don't think the CofD have mapped Int to IQ, but I know some of the older WoD books did.<br /> <br /> And despite all the issues with IQ as a metric, it's worth noting that 60 should be a very small portion of the population. IQ is gauged on a normal curve with a standard deviation of 15. That means 68% of the population should be between 85 and 115, and 95% of the population should be between 70 and 130. Only 0.15% of the population should have an IQ of 55 or less.<br /> <br /> For any attribute, a character that's in the 2.5% of the population that's below two standard deviations from mean is probably not a functional character for the games the CofD is aimed at; and the edge cases are all best handled by Conditions because they're going to involved more situational issues. Modelling someone with such a low IQ really doesn't work by just having low Intelligence score (because among other issues IQ doesn't measure generic intelligence well), and should really come out in ways Conditions handle best. An Intelligence 1/Academics 5 character operates just as well as an Intelligence 3/Academics 3 and Intelligence 5/Academics 1 character for the same roll. It becomes a purely descriptive difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T17:53:33-07:00","id":952173,"title":"","content":"*Ponders a persistent condition labelled &quot;mental retardation&quot;.*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T18:06:49-07:00","id":952182,"title":"","content":"And moving really disadvantageous qualities to conditions removes certain stigma from leaving a stat at 1, thus inviting bigger variety in possible builds --&gt; potentially wider play experience. I honestly think it's a solution that plays to the strongest points of the current iteration of the rules (that still, IMHO, underuse Condition system)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T18:11:13-07:00","id":952184,"title":"","content":"I mean, if your group is cool with having that in play, and you think you can do it respectfully... why not?<br /> <br /> It's just a very touchy subject that I don't think most groups really want to explore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T18:28:49-07:00","id":952190,"title":"","content":"Think Pakleds from Star Trek.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T21:23:48-07:00","id":952276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950626-what-would-a-person-with-one-dot-of-intelligence-but-four-dots-of-wits-be-like#post950626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just for fun, they also have five dots of firearms and a firearms specialty in 'theory'.</div> </div> </div> </div>The textbook example of &quot;street smart, not book smart.&quot; This person would be fast on their feet and hyper-observant, good at improvisation but terrible about anything logical or in need of time to solve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T06:28:31-07:00","id":952466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950626-what-would-a-person-with-one-dot-of-intelligence-but-four-dots-of-wits-be-like?p=952173#post952173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Ponders a persistent condition labelled &quot;mental retardation&quot;.*</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">\u200bThe proper term to use (as of the DSM-V) is &quot;Intellectual Disability&quot;, or one may also use &quot;Intellectual Developmental Disorder&quot;. Avoid using loaded terms. Thanks.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T01:40:44-07:00","id":953043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950626-what-would-a-person-with-one-dot-of-intelligence-but-four-dots-of-wits-be-like?p=952184#post952184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, if your group is cool with having that in play, and you think you can do it respectfully... why not?<br /> <br /> It's just a very touchy subject that I don't think most groups really want to explore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. I am currently in a game with a person whose character has a panic disorder and autism - pretty sure they utilise a condition for the panic disorder that rolls Resolve + Composure or they have panic attacks. It's working fine.<br /> <br /> The player is doing a superb job at it, and isn't doing it in a tasteless way, so it's perfectly fine IMO.<br /> <br /> But, obviously, it's up to each individual group with what they feel comfortable portraying. Admittedly, the group I am with doesn't seem to shy away from any subject, and although I find that fun and am comfortable exploring prickly topics, others aren't. YMMV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}